From: caomengxuan666 <2507560089@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:17:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(niu): apply the fork's npm, CI and script delta on
 the new base

Everything the fork owns outside codex-rs is either new upstream (the niu
workflows, scripts/niu, RELEASE.md) or a small semantic delta that upstream has
since reformatted, so the npm files are taken from upstream and the fork's real
intent is re-applied on top rather than reverted wholesale:

- `@openai/codex` -> `@cmx666/codex` throughout codex-cli, plus the repository
  URL and package name in codex-cli/package.json. The whitespace-insensitive
  diff showed the fork's 249/453/22-line rewrites were line endings and
  formatting around this rename.
- Upstream's newer codex-cli is kept, including the `vp` (Vite+) install-manager
  branch and the pnpm 10.34.5 bump.
- Upstream's Vite+ detection read `packages/@openai/codex.json` while asserting
  the recorded name is `@cmx666/codex`, so it could never match for this fork.
  Renamed that path to match.

The niu workflows are taken as-is; the release-version guard and the sccache
changes from the previous branch are unchanged.
